# R8 keep rules for Third Coast Sailing (release builds).
# AGP combines every *.keep file in src/main/keepRules and passes it to R8, together with the default Android rules
# (equivalent to proguard-android-optimize.txt) and the rules libraries ship in their AARs (MapLibre has its own).
# See https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/keep-rules-overview

# ---- Crash reports: keep file names and line numbers so stack traces can be traced back to the source
# (the names R8 shortens are restored from mapping.txt, which Android Studio writes next to the build and puts in
# the .aab for Google Play).
-keepattributes SourceFile,LineNumberTable
-renamesourcefileattribute SourceFile

# ---- Kotlin text functions: the 0.7 release crashed on start with IllegalAccessError in kotlin.text (called from
# Polar.parse). That build only optimized some packages (packageScope); the whole app is optimized now, which should
# avoid it, but kotlin.text is kept as it is for safety. Small cost; remove after a few releases without problems.
-keep class kotlin.text.** { *; }

# ---- Map engine: MapLibre's native (C++) code calls back into its Java classes by name. MapLibre ships its own keep
# rules; keeping all of it as well costs some size but rules out a map that fails to draw in release builds only.
-keep class org.maplibre.** { *; }
-dontwarn org.maplibre.**

# ---- Saved settings: enum constant names are written to the phone (e.g. the celestial skill level and sight
# conditions, read back with valueOf), so the app's enum names must not change between versions.
-keepclassmembers enum com.thirdcoastsailing.app.** { <fields>; }
